{{- /*
Render every enabled feature registered for one slot, in weight order.

@context {string} slot The slot name, such as "page.meta".
@context {page} page The page being rendered.

Every key this theme reads sits under one namespace, which Hugo asks
theme authors to do so that a site's own params and a second theme's
cannot collide with them. index, not dot notation, because a slug may
carry a hyphen and is then not a valid template identifier.

A slot no feature registers for is the common case, and it costs one
lookup here.

A component lives in a directory the site mounts, and a site that has
not mounted it does not have its partial. Not mounting it is how a
component is turned off, so its absence is an answer rather than a
fault. A toggle is part of the theme and is always there, so a missing
one still fails the build.

@example: {{ partial "slot.html" (dict "slot" "page.meta" "page" .) }}
*/ -}}
{{- $slot := .slot }}
{{- $page := .page }}
{{- with index (partialCached "slot-map.html" "features") $slot }}
  {{- $on := partialCached "feature-set.html" $page $page.RelPermalink }}
  {{- range . }}
    {{- if and (index $on .name) (or (not .kinds) (in .kinds $page.Kind)) }}
      {{- if or (ne .level "component") (templates.Exists (printf "_partials/%s" .partial)) }}
        {{- partial .partial $page }}
      {{- end }}
    {{- end }}
  {{- end }}
{{- end }}
